    <h1>About<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>I’m Martin, a distributed systems engineer based in Slovakia. I work with Rust, OCaml, and Solidity, with a focus on zero-knowledge rollups and the infrastructure around them.</p>
    <p>I’m a founding engineer and CTO at Zeko, a Mina-based ZK rollup. My hands-on work spans sequencing, proof orchestration, and Ethereum settlement.</p>
    <p>Before Zeko, I worked on account abstraction and EVM infrastructure at Milkomeda, co-founded the privacy-preserving federated learning project FELT Labs, and built software at Vacuumlabs.</p>
    <p>I studied software engineering at the Czech Technical University in Prague. This site is a place to share what I learn while building systems, along with case studies of the work itself.</p>
